  "body": "Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), brief q05 (40 x 40 x 100 block on a Tormach 770MX + microARC 4), CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release; reproduced by hand.\n\n## What happens\n\n```\nimport_model {\"name\": \"q05-4axis\", \"path\": \".../q05-4axis.step\"}\nload_machine {\"builtin\": \"Tormach 770MX + microARC 4\"}\nset_stock {\"axis\": \"x\", \"box\": {\"dx\": 44, \"dy\": 44, \"dz\": 110}}\nadd_tool {\"catalog\": \"DR-0600\", \"name\": \"6mm Drill\"}\nadd_setup {\"name\": \"Setup1\"}; add_setup {\"name\": \"Setup2\", \"datum_from\": \"Setup1\"}\nlay_part_on_face {\"setup\": \"Setup2\", \"face\": {\"model\": \"q05-4axis\", \"id\": \"face:0x9a06666bad6a627f\"}, \"plane\": \"g17\", \"place\": false}   -> \"turned X -90°\"\nadd_operation {\"kind\": \"drill\", \"name\": \"D\", \"source\": \"q05-4axis\", \"tool\": \"6mm Drill\"}\ndetect_holes {\"name\": \"D\"}   -> {\"holes\": 2, \"radial_holes\": 1, \"skipped\": [], \"undersize\": []}\ngenerate {\"name\": \"D\"}       -> D: invalid machining parameters: this op lists Z holes AND cross holes - drill either the mill's holes or the turret's, not both (M5.2 v1)\nedit_operation {\"name\": \"D\", \"params\": {\"cross\": []}}   -> bad params patch: unknown field cross - a drill operation has no field \"cross\"; see list_operation_types\n```\n\nThe \"radial hole\" is the Ø20 x 2 mm counterbore on the face that points down in this setup (`dir [0,0,1], origin [50,0,-20], radius 10`). It goes into `params.drill.cross`, a list for live-tooling cross holes on a turret, on a machine that has no turret. `undersize` stays empty although Ø20 > the Ø6 drill. `cross` is not in list_operation_types and edit_operation refuses it, so the operation can only be deleted and its holes typed in by hand.\n\n## Expected\n\nOn a mill, `detect_holes` keeps only the holes the tool can reach along the setup's Z (here the two Ø6 front holes) and names the others in `skipped`; any list it fills can be edited or cleared through edit_operation.\n\n## Repro files\n\n[q05-4axis.step](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/q05-4axis.step); agent report [REPORT.md](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/REPORT.md) problem 3. Related: #2601 (opposite radial holes merged).\n\nDone means: the steps above give a Drill op with the 2 front holes and the counterbore in `skipped`, and it generates (pinned by a test); `cross` is either editable or never filled on a machine without a turret.\n",
